{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MobiusRegulator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Filter.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.regulator_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.regulator_shift","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L185-L207","doc":"**The finite part is free.**  Given any regulator `R` of the admissible\nshape (a function of `(ε, length)` only) and any target shift `k`, the\nregulator `R' = R − k` has the same shape, differs from `R` by a constant (so\nhas the same divergent part), and moves the energy of *every* curve on which\nthe `R`-limit exists by exactly `k`.  Hence no value of an additive\nclassical-limit constant follows from the energy density `A` alone: it is\nfixed only by choosing the regulator's finite part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhw_minus_minimalSubtraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhw_minus_minimalSubtraction","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L173-L183","doc":"**The classical \"4\" is the finite part of the BFHW regulator.**  For every\ncurve of positive length on which both regularized limits exist,\n`E_BFHW(γ) = E_ms(γ) + 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhw_sub_ms_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhw_sub_ms_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L163-L171","doc":"For `l > 0`, `R_BFHW(ε,l) − R_ms(ε,l) → −4` as `ε → 0⁺` (it equals `−4`\nfor every `ε > 0`, by (a)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.msRegulator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.msRegulator","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L160-L161","doc":"The bare pole subtraction (\"minimal subtraction\"): `2l/ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhwRegulator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhwRegulator","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L156-L158","doc":"The BFHW regulator: the arc-distance integral of eq. (3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.regEnergy_sub_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.regEnergy_sub_indep","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L139-L152","doc":"**Independence of the curve.**  If `R₁ − R₂ → c` at every length, the\nenergy difference is the same number for any two curves on which all four\nlimits exist. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.regEnergy_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.regEnergy_sub","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L124-L137","doc":"**Regulator universality for `regEnergy`.**  For a curve `γ` on which both\nregularized limits exist, `E_{R₁}(γ) − E_{R₂}(γ) = −c` where\n`c = lim (R₁ − R₂)(ε, L(γ))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.regulator_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.regulator_difference","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L105-L122","doc":"**Regulator universality, limit form.**  If `A_ε(γ) − R₁(ε,L) → E₁`,\n`A_ε(γ) − R₂(ε,L) → E₂`, and `R₁(ε,L) − R₂(ε,L) → c` as `ε → 0⁺`, then\n`E₁ − E₂ = −c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.regEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.regEnergy","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L99-L103","doc":"The regularized energy of a curve `γ` for regulator `R : ε → length → ℝ`:\n`lim_{ε→0⁺} (A ε − R ε L)`, as a `limUnder` (meaningful when the limit exists). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhw_regularization_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhw_regularization_term","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L88-L93","doc":"**BFHW eq. (3), the signed term.**  The arc-distance term enters\n`E_ε(γ)` (eq. (1)) with a minus sign; its contribution is `4 − 2l/ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhw_regularization_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.bfhw_regularization_integral","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L74-L86","doc":"**BFHW eq. (3), the integral as printed.**  For a closed curve of\narclength `l > 0` and cutoff `ε > 0`,\n`∫₀^l [2 ∫_ε^{l/2} v⁻² dv] du = 2l/ε − 4`.  (BFHW work with `ε < l/2`; the\noriented interval integral makes the identity hold for every `ε > 0`, so that\nhypothesis is not needed and is not assumed.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MobiusRegulator.integral_inv_sq_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MobiusRegulator.integral_inv_sq_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MobiusRegulator.lean#L54-L72","doc":"Inner integral: `∫_ε^{b} v⁻² dv = 1/ε − 1/b` for `0 < ε`, `0 < b`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}